WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.834
-Well, Republicans in the House
finally elected a speaker

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.501
post-midnight early on Saturday

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.734
after Kevin McCarthy
acquiesced to the demands

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:09.601
of the most extreme
members of his caucus,

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:13.000
the same people who tried
to overthrow the 2020 election,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
in a stunning
and humiliating turn of events

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.801
that nearly led to a physical
brawl on the House floor

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.801
and almost certainly
portends nonstop chaos

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.000
for the next two years.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.000
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:29.167
It took four days and 15 tries.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.834
But Republicans were finally
able to elect a speaker

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.767
early on Saturday morning
just after midnight.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.133
This is the first time
in a century

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.567
it's taken more than one ballot

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.267
to elect a speaker,
never mind 15.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.734
But when it was
all said and done,

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.667
Republicans reacted like they
had just won the Super Bowl.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:47.133
-The Honorable Kevin McCarthy
of the state of California,

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:50.501
having received a majority
of the votes cast,

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:54.033
is duly elected Speaker
of the House of Representatives.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.868
[ Crowd chanting "USA!" ]

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.667
-Look, on one hand, I get it.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.801
I'd also break into applause
if it meant

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.901
I didn't have to spend
my Saturday with Matt Gaetz.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.200
"Hey, if you need
to run errands,

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.501
I can babysit your daughter."

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:16.667
"My daughter is 21.
She doesn't need a Gaetz."

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.834
That joke is based
on news reports.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.567
So, yeah, you're happy.
I get it.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.200
But that reaction
seems like a lot,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.234
considering it took you
four days and 15 tries

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:26.501
just to make one decision.

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:28.801
This is like if the Jets
pop champagne in the locker room

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:30.234
just for getting
their cleats on.

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:32.601
And if you're wondering, I'm not
feeling bitter toward the Jets

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:34.667
just because they eliminated
my Steelers

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:35.667
from playoff contention

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:37.167
by losing to the Dolphins
on Sunday,

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.767
even though everything else
that needed to happen

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.701
for the Steelers to snag
a playoff berth happened.

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.400
I did, however, take a swing

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.167
at our security guard Jim
this morning,

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:46.701
and he was very cool about it.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.200
He only broke one of my fingers.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.000
Though he did add, "There's more
where that came from,"

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.434
which I did not love hearing.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.868
It truly is absurd to watch
these doofuses celebrate

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.634
like they just landed
a rover on Mars

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.934
because they were finally able
to make one governing decision.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.033
The only time I've ever felt
that much relief

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.300
at someone making one decision

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.234
is when I go out
to dinner with my mom.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.868
"Mmmm.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.667
Should I have the chicken
or the fish?"

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:17.234
"Mom, we have been here
for four [bleep] days."

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:18.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.033
"I want the chicken,
but Lauren Boebert says

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:23.501
I should force the waiter to
read the specials one more time

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:25.133
because she doesn't want
to live in a country

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.234
where halibut is off the menu."

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:29.834
Now, as we told you last week,

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:31.934
before he finally won
on the 15th ballot,

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.434
McCarthy was stuck in a sort of
existential purgatory

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:37.667
where he just had to keep
sitting through losing votes

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:40.501
over and over again, because
until a speaker is chosen,

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.400
there's basically nothing else
that Congress can do,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.801
which meant that they had to
keep tallying up the votes.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.734
And the House clerk,
Cheryl Johnson,

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.167
who did a fantastic job,

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.901
had to keep announcing the
results the same way every time

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:52.300
until there was
finally a winner.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.734
-A speaker has not been elected.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.033
A speaker has not been elected.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.234
A speaker has not been elected.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.801
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.067
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:06.100
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.400
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.434
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:12.601
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.801
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:16.968
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.968
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.968
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.734
A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:27.200
The Honorable Kevin McCarthy
of the State of California,

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.567
having received a majority
of the votes cast,

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:34.667
is duly elected Speaker
of the House of Representatives.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.667
-We called her. We were like,
"Can you just one time

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.734
wear, like,
a super-goofy cowboy hat?

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.801
'Cause it'll make it
so funny in the montage."

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.534
This poor woman, for four days,
she wasn't the House clerk.

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:48.734
She was a hostage.

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:51.200
They should have made her
Speaker of the House.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.167
She did the Republicans a huge
favor, it should be noted,

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:56.501
by remaining calm and steadfast
and good at her job.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:58.634
She gave the proceedings
a level of decorum

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.234
they honestly didn't deserve.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:02.400
If that had been me up there, I
wouldn't have been able to say,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.901
"A speaker
has not been elected,"

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.667
in such a calm manner 14 times.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.667
I would have reacted
like Steve Harvey

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.501
when someone says something
really dumb on "Family Feud."

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.934
And, yeah, we do use clips

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:25.834
of Steve Harvey
on "Family Feud" a lot,

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.734
but only because
no one in the world

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:31.367
is better at their job
than he is at his.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:32.834
By the way, this all unfolded

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:34.434
into the late hours
of Friday night

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:35.534
and early Saturday morning.

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:36.734
Generally speaking,

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.467
that is not the sign
of a healthy democracy.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.901
Nothing good happens
after midnight on a Friday.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:43.334
If you're that old
and you're up after midnight,

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:46.434
you're probably drunk and buying
something real dumb off QVC.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:49.400
"Hello.
Yeah, I'd like to buy three

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.200
of the Victorian-style
porcelain doll lamps.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.367
And could you throw in

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.901
one of those portable
hand massagers, as well?

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:57.734
Yeah. My security guard
broke my finger.

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.734
I think he's gonna do it again!"

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.367
But, of course,
I couldn't help it.

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:04.200
I was up late
watching it all unfold.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.367
When I was a kid and I was
up late watching TV,

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:08.634
it used to be stuff like
horror movies or Cinemax

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:10.801
or, let's be honest,
"Taxicab Confessions."

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.400
Oh, yeah, baby.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.267
Give me 20 minutes
of an Eastern European couple

00:05:15.267 --> 00:05:18.000
in weird disco outfits
coming down from cocaine

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.100
and hitting on
a bemused cab driver.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.367
It wasn't much,
but before the Internet,

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.100
it was the closest
you could get to porn

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.734
without finding
a "Penthouse Forum"

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:29.767
in the woods behind the school.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:32.634
Now things are so insane
that if I'm up late watching TV,

00:05:32.634 --> 00:05:34.000
it's not soft-core porn.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.601
It's C-SPAN, because that
[bleep] has been hard-core.

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:40.701
If you were watching C-SPAN
as all this unfolded,

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:42.801
you got to see some tense
and surreal images

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.067
from a night
that was unprecedented

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:45.300
in American political history.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.200
Just to give you a taste
of what happened

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.934
before we get into
the blow by blow,

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:51.434
there was almost
a literal blow by blow

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.334
when one member
of the Republican caucus

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:56.400
had to be restrained by his face

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.601
so he couldn't
physically assault

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.133
another Republican member
of Congress.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:01.167
Look, at this.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:02.901
It's one thing
to hold a dude back

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:05.100
by his shoulders,
but by his face?

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.367
Is this the House
of Representatives

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.868
or a Long Island wedding?

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.467
"He ain't worth it, Tony.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:12.267
Come on, Tony.
This is Anthony's wedding.

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:15.167
Tony! Get Tony out of here
so he don't embarrass Anthony."

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:18.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.100
"He's having such a tough time
'cause the Jets are so lousy."

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:28.767
That was Republican congressman
Mike Rogers lunging after Gaetz,

00:06:28.767 --> 00:06:30.067
one of the last
remaining holdouts.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.133
Here's what a third
Republican member

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.667
who was in the middle
of the scrum

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.334
had to say about the near-brawl,

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:36.901
which should give you
a pretty good indication

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:39.033
of where the Republican Party
is at right now.

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:41.968
Again, this is one
of their fellow Republicans

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:43.801
describing what happened.

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:51.534
Now...

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:53.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:56.367
...I know that sounds like
a Jeff Foxworthy bit,

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:58.667
but actually it was

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:01.334
in the original draft
of the Constitution.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:05.634
Benjamin Franklin
was being super sassy

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:06.734
towards Thomas Jefferson

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:08.334
because Franklin lived
in Philadelphia

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:09.667
and Jefferson was from Virginia.

00:07:09.667 --> 00:07:11.634
Jefferson got drunk
one night and said,

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:16.033
"Any dumbass can fly a kite
in a lightning storm."

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:18.767
So then Franklin responded,
and this was his real voice,

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:20.133
because remember,
he lived in Philly.

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:21.300
[ Philadelphia accent ]
Youse guys should take it easy

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.100
on the booze
and drink some water.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:28.334
[ Normal voice ]
A lot of you jackals out there

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:29.400
are going to be like,
"Benjamin Franklin

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.701
wasn't born in Philadelphia.

00:07:30.701 --> 00:07:33.067
He lived in Boston.
He moved there when he was 17.

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:34.501
Why would he have
a Philly accent?"

00:07:34.501 --> 00:07:35.934
Well, 'cause if you
have a Boston accent

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:37.000
and you move to Philly,

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.834
they, like, chuck
[bleep] batteries at you.

00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:41.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:42.968
Whatever it was back --
like, horseshoes.

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:46.200
I don't know what --

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.434
Self-preservation.

00:07:47.434 --> 00:07:50.234
He said "wooter"
out of self-preservation.

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.467 --> 00:07:53.234
Friday night's drama
started with McCarthy

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:55.434
confidently predicting
that he had the votes

00:07:55.434 --> 00:07:58.234
to finally become speaker
after "acquisescing --

00:07:58.234 --> 00:07:59.801
after "acquisescing" --

00:07:59.801 --> 00:08:02.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.033 --> 00:08:04.300
After acquiescing to the demands

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:06.367
of the most extreme
members of his caucus.

00:08:06.367 --> 00:08:09.467
When reporters asked him
how he could be so confident,

00:08:09.467 --> 00:08:10.701
he had a simple answer.

00:08:12.467 --> 00:08:14.434
-Why are you confident
you have the votes?

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:18.701
-Oh.

00:08:18.701 --> 00:08:20.934
Can you?

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:22.634
Because the only person
in that chamber

00:08:22.634 --> 00:08:24.367
that I trust to count
is this lady.

00:08:24.367 --> 00:08:27.501
It's not exactly
confidence-inspiring

00:08:27.501 --> 00:08:29.934
when you're trying to become
second in line to the presidency

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:35.100
and your big brag is that you
share a skill with a Muppet.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.467
I can count.

00:08:36.467 --> 00:08:38.667
I have a sweet tooth.

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:42.501
And most of all,
me very ticklish.

00:08:42.501 --> 00:08:43.834
But you'll be shocked
to learn this.

00:08:43.834 --> 00:08:45.334
It turns out
McCarthy couldn't count,

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:47.667
because when Republicans got
to the floor on Friday night

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:49.834
for what they thought would be
their 14th and final ballot,

00:08:49.834 --> 00:08:51.667
they discovered midway
through the process

00:08:51.667 --> 00:08:53.067
that they didn't have the votes.

00:08:53.067 --> 00:08:56.200
That's when this truly
unprecedented scene took place,

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.300
with McCarthy walking over
to Gaetz on the House floor

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.901
during the voting
to confront him

00:09:00.901 --> 00:09:02.400
and get him to change his mind.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:03.901
And that confrontation ended

00:09:03.901 --> 00:09:06.334
with the now-infamous lunge
we showed you before.

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:09.133
Here is CNN's real-time
commentary of that moment

00:09:09.133 --> 00:09:12.467
as it unfolded live on national
television late on Friday night.

00:09:12.467 --> 00:09:15.701
-Kevin McCarthy walks off the --

00:09:15.701 --> 00:09:17.667
-He does not look happy.

00:09:17.667 --> 00:09:19.200
-He can change.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.067
-Yeah, somebody can change.

00:09:21.067 --> 00:09:23.300
-Kevin McCarthy
walks off the floor.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:24.968
-No, he's talking --
-I'm sorry.

00:09:24.968 --> 00:09:27.601
He walks up the floor, rather.

00:09:27.601 --> 00:09:29.501
Matt Gaetz.

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:34.067
He needed him to vote "yes,"
not "present."

00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:36.367
-This is it. I mean,
this is do or die for him.

00:09:36.367 --> 00:09:39.167
-This is quite a sight
to behold.

00:09:39.167 --> 00:09:42.934
Kevin McCarthy needs one vote
to become Speaker of the House.

00:09:42.934 --> 00:09:47.000
-Matt Gaetz does not look like
he is willing to acquiesce

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.868
and change his vote
from "present."

00:09:48.868 --> 00:09:52.067
-There's some guy in the back
who was --

00:09:52.067 --> 00:09:55.501
went out to yell at Gaetz
in a pink tie

00:09:55.501 --> 00:09:58.501
and another member
hold him back.

00:09:58.501 --> 00:10:01.033
-Look at that face.
-He looks dejected.

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:02.701
Look at that.

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:04.934
-It's like watching
a British nature documentary

00:10:04.934 --> 00:10:08.934
about those jacked kangaroos
who fight for dominance.

00:10:08.934 --> 00:10:10.834
[ British accent ] This is
quite a sight to behold.

00:10:10.834 --> 00:10:12.901
The alpha male
is approaching his rival

00:10:12.901 --> 00:10:15.334
with his chest puffed out,
and wait, what's this?

00:10:15.334 --> 00:10:17.667
The alpha male
is begging with his rival

00:10:17.667 --> 00:10:19.133
to please be nice to him.

00:10:19.133 --> 00:10:21.033
Quite a humiliating spectacle.

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:23.234
And now a third kangaroo,
described by his friends

00:10:23.234 --> 00:10:27.067
as a drunken redneck,
has entered the fray

00:10:27.067 --> 00:10:28.868
and is being restrained
by his face.

00:10:28.868 --> 00:10:30.367
[ Normal voice ]
And that was just one

00:10:30.367 --> 00:10:31.901
of the many crazy sequences

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:34.534
that were apparently happening
on the House floor Friday night.

00:10:34.534 --> 00:10:36.467
A photographer also captured
this incredible moment

00:10:36.467 --> 00:10:37.968
where Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:10:37.968 --> 00:10:39.767
held up her phone
to a colleague,

00:10:39.767 --> 00:10:41.567
and then he held up his hand

00:10:41.567 --> 00:10:43.033
to indicate
he didn't want the call.

00:10:43.033 --> 00:10:45.868
And when you zoom in, you can
see that the call is from DT,

00:10:45.868 --> 00:10:47.801
AKA Donald Trump.

00:10:47.801 --> 00:10:49.467
Trump must have been
so embarrassed

00:10:49.467 --> 00:10:52.300
by that pic of a Republican
not wanting to take his call.

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:54.033
Although knowing Trump,

00:10:54.033 --> 00:10:55.968
he'd probably claim
it wasn't him on the phone.

00:10:55.968 --> 00:10:58.234
[ As Trump ] The fake news is
saying Republicans ignored me,

00:10:58.234 --> 00:10:59.400
but that wasn't me calling.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.701
It was a different DT --

00:11:00.701 --> 00:11:02.701
the great David Tennant.

00:11:02.701 --> 00:11:04.534
[ Laughter ]

00:11:04.534 --> 00:11:05.868
Doctor Who himself.

00:11:05.868 --> 00:11:06.901
You know, some people --

00:11:06.901 --> 00:11:08.467
some people say his name
is The Doctor,

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:11.634
but I like to say Doctor Who.

00:11:11.634 --> 00:11:14.067
A friend came up to me once,

00:11:14.067 --> 00:11:16.901
big guy, strong guy, giant nerd,
tears pouring down his face.

00:11:16.901 --> 00:11:18.767
And he said to me, "Sir,
have you seen the doctor?"

00:11:18.767 --> 00:11:20.667
And I said, "Doctor Who."
And he said, "The doctor."

00:11:20.667 --> 00:11:22.133
And I said,
"I know, Doctor Who."

00:11:22.133 --> 00:11:25.100
And he said, "The doctor,"
and we went back and forth,

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.200
back and forth in circles
like that for hours.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.801
This was on January 6th,
by the way.

00:11:28.801 --> 00:11:32.400
It's one of the reasons I wasn't
answering calls for help,

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:35.100
because I was engaged in this
little silly vaudeville routine.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.968
It was a lot of fun, and in
the end, of course, third base.

00:11:37.968 --> 00:11:39.901
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.601 --> 00:11:43.634
[ Normal voice ] Now, McCarthy
finally acquiesced.

00:11:43.634 --> 00:11:46.100
Boy, he's really putting it
in there a lot today, isn't he?

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.834
[ Laughter ]

00:11:48.834 --> 00:11:52.868
God forbid we give in

00:11:52.868 --> 00:11:55.667
and find a synonym
for "acquiesced."

00:11:55.667 --> 00:11:57.267
[ Laughter ]

00:11:57.267 --> 00:11:59.868
Oh, no.
Sal wouldn't cave.

00:11:59.868 --> 00:12:01.968
[ Laughter ]

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.801
McCarthy finally acqui--
acquiesced.

00:12:08.801 --> 00:12:11.400
Oh, everybody at home
watching like,

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:14.067
"Oh, a [bleep] genius
must have written this."

00:12:14.067 --> 00:12:15.934
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.901 --> 00:12:22.734
McCarthy finally acquiesced
to a bunch of demands

00:12:22.734 --> 00:12:24.634
from the extreme holdouts
in his caucus,

00:12:24.634 --> 00:12:26.834
which we're still
finding out about now.

00:12:26.834 --> 00:12:28.801
But if you think this chaos
and hostage-taking

00:12:28.801 --> 00:12:30.133
means we're in for two years

00:12:30.133 --> 00:12:31.601
of nonstop dysfunction
in the House,

00:12:31.601 --> 00:12:33.567
Kevin McCarthy would like
to tell you you're wrong,

00:12:33.567 --> 00:12:35.033
because according to him,

00:12:35.033 --> 00:12:37.100
it was actually
a very valuable experience.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:39.033
-How do you expect
to govern this way

00:12:39.033 --> 00:12:41.968
if it has been taking this long
to get the conference united?

00:12:41.968 --> 00:12:43.667
-See, this is the great part.

00:12:43.667 --> 00:12:47.367
Because it took this long,
now we learned how to govern.

00:12:47.367 --> 00:12:49.434
[ Laughter ]

00:12:49.434 --> 00:12:51.734
-A week ago, I had no idea

00:12:51.734 --> 00:12:55.868
you could grab a congressman
by the face.

00:12:55.868 --> 00:12:57.501
But now I know -- we all know --

00:12:57.501 --> 00:13:01.934
it's a safe and effective way
of slowing them down.

00:13:01.934 --> 00:13:04.467
Things are doubtlessly going to
become increasingly unhinged,

00:13:04.467 --> 00:13:06.033
thanks to the concessions
McCarthy made

00:13:06.033 --> 00:13:07.501
to the extremists in his caucus.

00:13:07.501 --> 00:13:10.467
The next step for the House is
to vote on a new set of rules,

00:13:10.467 --> 00:13:11.701
which may happen
after this taping.

00:13:11.701 --> 00:13:13.133
We're not sure, and sadly,

00:13:13.133 --> 00:13:15.601
C-SPAN will have to go back
to its normal way of operating

00:13:15.601 --> 00:13:18.000
by using only
government-controlled cameras.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.100
While this whole thing
dragged on,

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:20.834
C-SPAN could do
whatever it wanted

00:13:20.834 --> 00:13:22.100
and without any constraints.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:26.200
C-SPAN was like watching
Teen Wolf play basketball.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.767
And now, with the moon
no longer full,

00:13:27.767 --> 00:13:29.534
it's just a 5'6" point guard

00:13:29.534 --> 00:13:31.167
who can shoot free throws
and that's about it.

00:13:31.167 --> 00:13:32.868
Do we still love you, C-SPAN?
Sure.

00:13:32.868 --> 00:13:36.033
But we will never forget
your incredible week

00:13:36.033 --> 00:13:37.267
of furry-ass dunks.

00:13:37.267 --> 00:13:40.033
Now, sadly, we're going to
go back to the days

00:13:40.033 --> 00:13:42.434
of barely being able to hear
what happens on C-SPAN,

00:13:42.434 --> 00:13:45.300
because whenever someone
in the C-SPAN control room

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.000
asks to jack up the volume,

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.501
someone else
informs them that...

00:13:48.501 --> 00:13:51.200
-A speaker has not been elected.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.734
[ Laughter ]

00:13:52.734 --> 00:13:54.300
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:56.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

